{
  "comment": [
    "UNION ALL phase 2: the public API and strict branch result compatibility.",
    "",
    "Six classes, not a campaign. The milestone is not frozen and this is not the",
    "UNION manifest — it is the focused set that attacks the rules phase 2 actually",
    "introduced: the one comparison authority, the shape a composed query carries,",
    "the shape a nested union carries, and the two guards that keep a query with no",
    "result out of a set operation. Everything else about UNION ALL — sources, CTEs,",
    "writes, ordering, the integration matrix — has no rules here yet and therefore",
    "nothing to mutate.",
    "",
    "Kept apart from manifest.json and uuidmanifest.json on purpose. Those two have",
    "closed accounting, and merging a batch that will grow into either of them would",
    "reopen a total that is already evidence.",
    "",
    "Every killer runs in the root module and needs no database: what these classes",
    "attack is decided when a union is built, before any statement exists. The",
    "server-side proof that the resulting statements run is in",
    "internal/gendemo/m16_union_test.go, which is not part of this campaign."
  ],
  "evidence_commit": "ab3e1df",
  "evidence_commit_note": [
    "ab3e1df is the revision every UNION ALL class was last applied to and run at, in a",
    "worktree checked out at exactly that commit, with the manifests read and written",
    "outside it so the tree stayed clean between classes. It is kept reachable as",
    "archive/m16-union-mutation-evidence.",
    "",
    "The five UNION ALL campaigns were rerun together at one revision after `mutate",
    "anchors` found four anchors that later phases had silently invalidated by editing",
    "the code they quote. An anchor that no longer matches makes its class look like a",
    "survivor, so the campaigns were pinned to revisions where they no longer ran.",
    "They run again, and three harness controls were active: anchors still quote their",
    "code, every site names the function its anchor is inside, and each semantic probe",
    "survives every mutation in another function."
  ],
  "classes": [
    {
      "id": "P2-1",
      "batch": "P2",
      "name": "Two branches stop having to agree on the Go type of a result column",
      "mutation": {
        "file": "resultshape.go",
        "anchor": "unionclasses/P2-1/anchor.txt",
        "replacement": "unionclasses/P2-1/replacement.txt",
        "count": 1,
        "expresses": [
          "The one comparison authority stops looking at the Go type each slot is",
          "read into, so a branch selecting int32 is accepted against a first branch",
          "selecting int64 and the scanner reads a value the column cannot hold."
        ]
      },
      "precondition": {
        "expect": [
          "TestUnionMutationPrecondition/P2-1"
        ],
        "argv": [
          "go",
          "test",
          "-json",
          "-count=1",
          ".",
          "-run",
          "^TestUnionMutationPrecondition$/^P2-1$"
        ]
      },
      "semantic": {
        "expect": [
          "TestCompare_refusesEveryMismatchWithoutWidening"
